                              "source": [
                                        "# Time-series cross-validation & Hyperparameter tuning\n",
                                        "This section reuses the training window above (`train_test_label`), the same features (`FEATURE_COLS`) and the same five classifiers. Its objective is to perform cross validation using:\n",
                                        "\n",
                                        "1. **A chronological hold-out.** The newest 30 days of the window are the test set. The random stratified split above mixes later orders into training, which can't happen in operation.\n",
                                        "2. **Time-series CV on the remaining days.** There are 5 expanding-window folds. Each fold trains on earlier approval days and validates on later ones, with a 45-day gap. Training labels must already be known at the validation start date, and no approval day is split.\n",
                                        "\n",
                                        "The reusable code lives in `src/tuning.py`. The tuned parameters and thresholds are saved to `results/classification_tuning.json`.\n",
                                        "\n",
                                        "Run time is about 5 minutes on 4 cores. Every model uses `n_jobs=1`, so the parallelism happens across CV folds and the CPU isn't oversubscribed."
                              ]
                    },
                    {
                              "cell_type": "markdown",
                              "id": "35dc9ea6",
                              "metadata": {},
                              "source": [
                                        "This section conducts time-series cross validation based on the default parameters used in the earlier section, as well as using the same run date of 2018-06-02 (i.e. June 2018 Model)"
                              ]
                    },
                    {
                              "cell_type": "code",
                              "execution_count": 29,
